From 9d19931df73ddf3032eaeaaad9cf92ecbd983a03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhaosiying12138 <neucszhaopeng2016@163.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 23:16:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 34/42] gpu-compute: count LGKM for group-segment work on
 non-memory units

Wavefront::reserveResources() tests isALU()/isNop() before isLocalMem(), so a
DS instruction that also carries those semantics is routed to a SIMD unit
rather than to the LDS memory unit. ScheduleStage only performs
incLGKMInstsIssued() in its memory-unit loop, so such an instruction is never
counted at issue, yet every DS execute() retires exactly one LGKM count. The
wave's outstanding counter then underflows.

In the Vega set two instructions hit this: ds_swizzle_b32 (Load|ALU, which
deliberately omits MemoryRef because it never touches DS storage) and ds_nop
(Nop). Hardware makes both observable through s_waitcnt lgkmcnt, so the repair
is to count them at issue rather than to drop the retire, which would let a
dependent s_waitcnt fall through while the destination VGPR is still in
flight.

Count group-segment, non-scalar work in the non-memory scheduling loop. The
predicate is a segment property, not an instruction name: GroupSegment is set
only by Inst_DS, so it covers any future DS instruction that acquires ALU or
Nop semantics, and it cannot match ordinary VALU or SALU work.

Evidence retains an A/B on one public-HIP capsule built around
__builtin_amdgcn_ds_swizzle, which reproduces the panic in about two minutes
instead of the forty minute model run that first exposed it. The pre-fix
binary aborts with "retired an LGKM instruction that was not outstanding
(count 0)"; the rebuilt binary completes the dispatch and synchronises. The
capsule also records that gem5 applies no permutation for
swizzle(QUAD_PERM,3,2,1,0); that is a separate defect, not addressed here.

Checkpoint-ID: CP-0058
Goal-ID: GSIM-001
Plan-Revision: 16
Source-Lock-SHA256: 8c0a6d1d04d5a73ab036ddc56d09ff59f7513077931868bdfac5a763f85a73d4
Evidence-Manifest-SHA256: d61ffdc405040587694381549794fc05260a1839848a149c8ceaf252ec8ddc1b
Change-Kind: bugfix
Baseline-Commit: 30d2511083d7c32ffa75ef1fd1864432c3212cf8
---
 src/gpu-compute/schedule_stage.cc | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gpu-compute/schedule_stage.cc b/src/gpu-compute/schedule_stage.cc
index 0d54df1e7..48af8936c 100644
--- a/src/gpu-compute/schedule_stage.cc
+++ b/src/gpu-compute/schedule_stage.cc
@@ -181,6 +181,20 @@ ScheduleStage::exec()
             // this wave spends in SCH stage.
             wf->stats.schCycles++;
             stats.addToSchListStalls[j]++;
+        } else if (gpu_dyn_inst->isGroupSeg() && !gpu_dyn_inst->isScalar()) {
+            // A group-segment (LDS) instruction normally reserves a memory
+            // execution unit and is counted by the memory loop above. One
+            // that also carries ALU or Nop semantics -- ds_swizzle_b32 and
+            // ds_nop -- is routed to a SIMD unit by
+            // Wavefront::reserveResources() instead, because isALU()/isNop()
+            // are tested before isLocalMem(). Its execute() still retires
+            // exactly one LGKM count, and the hardware likewise makes it
+            // observable through s_waitcnt lgkmcnt, so it must be counted at
+            // issue here. Without this the wave's outstanding count
+            // underflows and a later s_waitcnt falls through while the
+            // destination VGPR is still in flight.
+            wf->incLGKMInstsIssued();
+            wf->trackLGKMInst(gpu_dyn_inst);
         }
     }
 
